course: dictionary
lesson: 11718
title: What is real?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Authenticity means being real or genuine, not fake or copied. «The museum checked the authenticity of the old coin before it went on display.» The experts wanted to be sure the coin was truly old and not a copy.
explain: You can also use authenticity about people. Being true to yourself means acting in a sincere, honest way instead of pretending. «Mia's authenticity made her friends trust her, because she always said what she really thought.»
explain: Look for useful phrases: «check the authenticity», «prove its authenticity» and «a certificate of authenticity». Each one is about showing that something is real. The adjective you may already know is authentic, so if something is authentic, it has authenticity.
fact: Authenticity means being real or genuine, not fake or copied.
fact: Authenticity is an uncountable noun, so we do not add an s to it: we say «the authenticity», not «the authenticitys».
fact: «A certificate of authenticity» is a paper that proves an item, such as a painting or a watch, is real.
fact: When you talk about people, authenticity means being true to yourself and honest, rather than pretending to be someone else.
fact: Online, you can check the authenticity of a website, email or photo by asking: is it really from who it says it is, and is the picture real or edited?
exercise: «The expert studied the painting to check its authenticity.» What does authenticity mean here? | Being hung on a wall | *Being real, not a fake copy | Being painted by a child | Being very expensive
exercise: Maya's friend says, «Be yourself, Maya: your authenticity is what makes you special.» What does authenticity mean here? | Wearing the most fashionable clothes | Copying what other people do | Hiding your real feelings | *Being true to yourself and honest
exercise: You get an email that says it is from your bank. Which question helps you check its authenticity? | *Is it really from the bank it says it is? | Does it have a picture of a cat in it? | Is the writing in bold? | Is it a long email?
test: «The shop gave her a certificate of authenticity with the watch.» What does a certificate of authenticity prove? | That the watch is blue | *That the watch is real | That the watch is new and in a box | That the watch is cheap
test: Ben wants to prove the authenticity of the old letter. What does «prove its authenticity» mean? | To throw it away | To make a copy of it | To make it longer | *To show that it is real and genuine
exam: «Ella's authenticity shows when she says what she really thinks.» What does authenticity mean in this sentence? | Having lots of friends | Pretending to be someone else | Being quiet in class | *Being honest and true to herself
